  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN- REDD Global Agreement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to United Nations Collaborative Programme on Reduced Emissions from Deforestation and Degradation in Developing Countries (cooperation betw FAO, UNDP and UNEP).

The current phase of the UN-REDD programme builds on the same two main components as the previous phase (2016-2021): 1) Technical Assistance (TA) to forest countries and 2) a Global Knowledge Management (GKM) component. These two components entail the provision of the best technical expertise and policy support from the Participation UN-organizations across all areas of REDD+. The TA component consist of providing technical assistance to forest countries by experts within different areas in the three UN-organizations. The UN-REDD programme also has a focus on ensuring a meaningful role of new financing opportunities, focusing on  ART/TREES and the LEAF coalition.</narrative>
  </description>
